      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Global evaluation of CDNs performance using PlanetLab",
      "publisher": "UPCommons institutional repository (Universitat Politècnica de Catalunya)",
      "author": "Pais Cereghetti; Andrés Nicolás",
      "published_at": "2012-11-19",
      "url": "https://openalex.org/W91851452",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T16:07:07.666Z",
      "sha256": "7ea47dad4e4386e5400ff29612abe3ed06ca236f821466cd41ade035a7dab835",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "These\\ntechniques aim to avoid fetching web objects from origin web server, especially\\nin “heavy” objects such as multimedia files.\\nCDN provides not only a clever way of distributing content in a globally, but\\nalso preventing problems such as the “flash crowd events”.",
        "This best server\\nselection employs a technique based on DNS with the objective of mapping the\\nIP address with the best available server in terms of latency.\\nThe current project presents a global performance of Akamai server selection\\ntechnique using tools such as PlanetLab and Httperf.",
        "Different tests were done\\nwith the objective of comparing the results of the global distributed users to\\nidentify those areas where Akamai perform in a suitable way.",
        "To determinate\\nthis, the results obtained with Akamai were also compared with a non-CDN\\ndistribution web page.",
        "Finally a linear correlation between the latencies\\nmeasured and the number of hops was identified."
